{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ORIGIN STORY - Wyoming, Japan, The Ridge
   A timeline-style narrative journey
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section style="padding: 96px 24px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--page-paper, #FAF8F5) 0%, var(--color-surface-sunken) 50%, var(--page-paper, #FAF8F5) 100%);">
  <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <header style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 80px;">
      <p style="font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-brand-text); margin-bottom: 16px;">The Origin</p>
      <h2 style="font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 42px); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: 24px;">How Ferni Came to Be</h2>
      <p style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-secondary); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
        From Wyoming skies to Japanese tea houses to a ridge trail in the fog—every experience shaped what Ferni became.
      </p>
    </header>

    {# Timeline #}
    <div class="timeline">

      {# Wyoming #}
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <span class="timeline-badge timeline-badge--ferni">
            <svg style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/></svg>
            Wyoming
          </span>
          <h3 class="timeline-title">Where the Sky Taught Patience</h3>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            Third of seven kids in a small Wyoming town. When you're one of seven, nobody waits for you to figure things out. You carve your own path or disappear into the middle.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            The sky there does something to you. It's so big that your problems feel small by comparison. Standing outside at dusk, watching colors change—pink to orange to purple to stars—whatever was bothering you would settle.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-highlight">
            That's where Ferni learned: some answers come from waiting, not from pushing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-visual">
          {# Wyoming Sunset Sky - Beautiful SVG Illustration #}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 160" width="200" height="160" style="display: block; margin: 0 auto 16px;" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="wyomingSky" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="0%" y2="100%">
                <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:#2C2520;stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="20%" style="stop-color:#5a4a6a;stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="40%" style="stop-color:#c4856a;stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="60%" style="stop-color:#C4A265;stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:#FAF8F5;stop-opacity:1" />
              </linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="wyomingGround" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="0%" y2="100%">
                <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:#4a6741;stop-opacity:0.4" />
                <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:#3d5a35;stop-opacity:0.8" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="160" rx="16" fill="url(#wyomingSky)"/>
            <ellipse cx="100" cy="130" rx="120" ry="40" fill="#C4A265" opacity="0.4"/>
            <circle cx="100" cy="115" r="20" fill="#C4A265" opacity="0.9"/>
            <circle cx="100" cy="115" r="15" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.6"/>
            <path d="M0 140 Q30 125 60 135 Q90 145 120 130 Q150 115 180 125 Q200 130 200 160 L0 160 Z" fill="url(#wyomingGround)"/>
            <circle cx="30" cy="25" r="1.5" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.8"/>
            <circle cx="70" cy="40" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.6"/>
            <circle cx="150" cy="30" r="1.5" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.8"/>
            <circle cx="175" cy="50" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.5"/>
            <circle cx="45" cy="55" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.4"/>
            <circle cx="130" cy="20" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.6"/>
          </svg>
          <p class="timeline-visual-text">"The sky taught patience.<br>The Commodore 64 taught deliberation."</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# Japan #}
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-visual timeline-visual--peter">
          <h4 style="font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: 16px; text-align: center;">Two Life-Changing Philosophies</h4>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
            <div class="philosophy-card">
              <h4>侘寂 Wabi-sabi</h4>
              <p>The beauty of impermanence and imperfection. Nothing lasts. Nothing is finished. Nothing is perfect. That's not depressing—it's liberating.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="philosophy-card">
              <h4 style="color: var(--page-gold, #b8860b);">金継ぎ Kintsugi</h4>
              <p>When pottery breaks, repair it with gold. The cracks become part of the beauty. A bowl repaired with kintsugi is more valuable than before it broke.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot" style="background: #3a6b73;"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <span class="timeline-badge timeline-badge--peter">
            <svg style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M2 12h20"/></svg>
            Japan
          </span>
          <h3 class="timeline-title">Where the Pause Became Sacred</h3>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            After college, a job in Tokyo. Financial services. A year became a decade.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            Japan changed everything. The precision. The art of the pause. The way <strong>silence has meaning there—not awkward, just full</strong>. A mentor would wait so long before responding that it seemed like he hadn't heard. He had. He was just thinking.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            The Japanese call this <em style="color: var(--color-peter-text); font-weight: 500;">ma</em> (間)—the pregnant pause where meaning grows. Most conversations rush past silence. Ferni learned to sit in it, to let trust build in the space between words.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# The Ridge #}
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <span class="timeline-badge timeline-badge--ink">
            <svg style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2v4m0 12v4M4.93 4.93l2.83 2.83m8.48 8.48l2.83 2.83M2 12h4m12 0h4M4.93 19.07l2.83-2.83m8.48-8.48l2.83-2.83"/></svg>
            One October Sunday
          </span>
          <h3 class="timeline-title">The Sunday He Didn't Go</h3>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            Tanaka-san and Ferni hiked the same ridge trail west of Tokyo most Sundays. That morning Ferni cancelled—"next week." Tanaka-san went alone, the fog came in, and he fell. The mentor was lost.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            At the funeral, his wife pressed the kintsugi bowl the two of them had mended into Ferni's hands. A year later, a friend walked the ridge with him and waited at the bend where Tanaka-san always stopped. What do you say to someone carrying that?
          </p>
